        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0828" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg706"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Straus to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 22, 1888</date>.
                        (Received January 7, 1889.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 151.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the Bible
                    House has for several months past been seeking permission from the minister of
                    public instruction to print in Turkish thirty-live thousand Bible tracts,
                    consisting of the Psalms the Proverbs, the four Gospels, and the Acts.</p>
                <p>The minister of public instruction having declined to give the authorization, the
                    matter was referred to the legation by the Bible House.</p>
                <p>Yesterday I succeeded in having the grand vizier give orders for the necessary
                    authorization.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. S. Straus.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
